Mother smiles.
"How did you tell them that story?" Mother asks.
"Tell it to me once more."
I tell that story again, but very briefly this time.
"I came to Kochi in January."
"I called a taxi from the airport."
"The very first day, I saw Anitha."
Mother listens to everything happily.
"I remember that January morning," Mother says.
"At the Mexico airport, you said goodbye to us."
"You went inside."
"That day I felt great sadness."
"Your father and I stood there for a little while."
I listen to Mother's words carefully.
"But now, you found new friends there."
"When I hear that, I have great joy," Mother says.
